<title>USA: Nebraska housing $50 mln revs repriced - Lehman.</title>
<headline>Nebraska housing $50 mln revs repriced - Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said it repriced a $50 million Nebraska Investment Finance Agency single-family housing revenue bond issue, 1996 Series C, and cut yields by five basis points in the 1998 through 2002 maturities.  </p>
<p>NEBRASKA INVESTMENT FINANCE AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $50,000,000*</p>
<p>Single Family Housing Revenue Bonds</p>
<p>1996 Series C</p>
<p>We have the verbal award.</p>
<p>		  SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>MOODY'S: NAF		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>DATED: 05/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 09/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 09/01 &amp; 03/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		AMOUNT*   AMOUNT*   COUPON</p>
<p>			   (3/1)    (9/1)</p>
